You are implementing the "Try It On" virtual try-on feature for Alankara, a fabric/cloth
jewellery ecommerce brand. Follow /docs/tryon-architecture.md as the source of truth for
architecture, data model, and component structure — read it before writing code.

Hard constraints, do not violate:
1. All face/landmark detection and AR rendering must run 100% client-side in the browser
   (MediaPipe Face Landmarker via WASM/WebGL + Three.js). Never send camera frames or video
   to any backend automatically.
2. A customer photo/frame is only ever uploaded when they explicitly click "Share with
   Alankara" or "Share My Look" — implement this as a single, explicit, auditable action,
   not a side effect of any other flow.
3. Match the existing Alankara visual identity exactly: warm ivory, maroon, champagne gold,
   soft blush, elegant serif type, the existing flower logo. Do not introduce neon AR
   graphics, cyberpunk UI, blue gradients, or generic "tech dashboard" styling anywhere in
   this feature, including error and permission states.
4. Every earring **or necklace** product needs its own try-on calibration — never hardcode
   one placement for all products. Necklaces use a parallel shoulder/neck-base pipeline
   (`useNecklaceAnchors` + `NecklaceOverlayCanvas`), not ear anchors.
5. Provide manual correction controls (zoom/move/scale/rotate/reset) in photo mode, because
   automatic ear detection will not always be accurate.
6. Handle all error states gracefully with warm, on-brand copy (camera denied, no face
   detected, poor lighting, one ear only visible, unsupported browser/device) — always give
   the customer a fallback path, never a dead end.
7. Do not generate or alter product imagery with AI. The try-on asset must be the actual
   product's approved transparent PNG/WebP, uploaded by admin.
8. AI customization interpretation may only produce a structured suggestion for
   admin review — it must never modify or create an order on its own.

Work in the phases given to you one at a time. After each phase, stop and summarize what you
changed and what needs manual testing before continuing to the next phase.
